 small electronics and boutique retail gift sets.</td></tr><tr><th>Design note</th><td>Bag, box and insert should use one brand system: logo, color, finish and unboxing sequence.</td></tr><tr><th>Logistics note</th><td>Paper bags should be flat packed; foam inserts should be protected from compression and dust.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n  </section>\n  <section><h2>Complete packaging system</h2><p>Luxury packaging is not only the box. A paper gift bag, insert, tissue paper, label and carton packing plan can work together to create a more complete buyer experience.</p></section>\n  <section><h2>Production details</h2><p>Handle strength, glue area, bottom board and insert tolerance should be checked before mass production, especially for retail stores and gift campaigns.</p></section>\n<section class=\"rfq-checklist\"><h2>Procurement Checklist</h2><ol><li>Confirm whether paper bag must carry product weight or only support gifting.</li><li>Choose rope handle, ribbon handle, cotton handle or die-cut handle.</li><li>Send actual product sample or 3D file for foam insert cutout.</li><li>Check insert tolerance and surface scratch risk.</li><li>Request carton packing method for bag, insert and box together.</li></ol></section><section class=\"faq-block\"><h2>FAQ</h2><details><summary>What GSM is common for paper gift bags?</summary><p>The right GSM depends on bag size, product weight and finish, but buyers should confirm load capacity during sampling.</p></details><details><summary>Is foam insert better than paperboard insert?</summary><p>Foam insert is better for delicate or premium products, while paperboard insert is more economical and recyclable.</p></details><details><summary>Can BestPackFactory supply bags and inserts together?</summary><p>Yes. The site supports boxes, bags, inserts, labels and related packaging components as one B2B project.</p></details></section><section class=\"rfq-template-box\"><h2>CTA: Ask Lisa for a packaging strategy quote</h2><p>Send 